1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,797
Because of pressure, insecurity, things like that...

2
00:00:02,797 --> 00:00:06,407
Yeah, your family is so well-off—you're a rich kid.

3
00:00:06,407 --> 00:00:07,927
Why would you want me?

4
00:00:07,927 --> 00:00:10,127
There are so many great girls out there.

5
00:00:15,267 --> 00:00:20,257
I love traveling abroad. I love Japan's cherry blossoms and shrines.

6
00:00:20,297 --> 00:00:23,139
I prefer online games and figurines.

7
00:00:23,177 --> 00:00:25,874
I also play games at home

8
00:00:26,057 --> 00:00:28,216
And collect some figurines.

9
00:00:28,227 --> 00:00:30,217
Don't you find it interesting?

10
00:00:30,227 --> 00:00:34,807
Wow, I'm hopeless at games.

11
00:00:34,807 --> 00:00:35,807
I don't know how to play at all.

12
00:00:35,807 --> 00:00:37,797
I can teach you how to play games

13
00:00:37,807 --> 00:00:40,085
My Switch is still collecting dust.

14
00:00:40,097 --> 00:00:43,749
Really?

15
00:00:43,767 --> 00:00:45,667
I want to play

16
00:00:45,677 --> 00:00:46,677
I'll bring it next time.

17
00:00:46,677 --> 00:00:47,677
We could get Pokémon.

18
00:00:47,677 --> 00:00:50,145
Wow

19
00:00:50,157 --> 00:00:52,386
But I really like

20
00:00:52,397 --> 00:00:54,397
collecting those perfumes and shoes

21
00:00:54,397 --> 00:00:56,387
Because I think they're unique

22
00:00:56,397 --> 00:00:58,387
I don't really get that

23
00:00:58,397 --> 00:00:59,397
But I like listening to pop music

24
00:00:59,397 --> 00:01:01,387
I think pop music is unique too

25
00:01:01,397 --> 00:01:04,123
Hmm, that's true

26
00:01:04,137 --> 00:01:06,137
But I prefer classical music

27
00:01:06,137 --> 00:01:08,127
What's so good about classical music?

28
00:01:08,137 --> 00:01:09,367
You like to eat...

29
00:01:09,367 --> 00:01:10,367
I'm a bank manager

30
00:01:10,367 --> 00:01:12,277
Now we're suddenly talking about jobs.

31
00:01:12,277 --> 00:01:13,277
I'm a security guard

32
00:01:13,357 --> 00:01:16,327
Brecht?

33
00:01:16,370 --> 00:01:20,880
Think it over.

34
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:24,388
I can secretly watch the monitors

35
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:26,530
I can see you anytime

36
00:01:26,530 --> 00:01:28,546
Don't you feel safe?

37
00:01:28,570 --> 00:01:29,910
It gives me a sense of security.

38
00:01:29,910 --> 00:01:31,330
Then can I install one

39
00:01:31,330 --> 00:01:32,470
in your security booth too?

40
00:01:32,470 --> 00:01:33,590
I'll watch you anytime too

41
00:01:33,590 --> 00:01:36,600
But if, in that security booth,

42
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:40,300
you put on a show every day—

43
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:41,260
if you performed—

44
00:01:41,260 --> 00:01:42,560
that might be interesting.

45
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:43,980
If you're just sitting there

46
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,120
I can perform for you

47
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:46,760
We can video call all day

48
00:01:46,760 --> 00:01:47,920
I have plenty of time

49
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:48,740
But I still have to work

50
00:01:48,740 --> 00:01:51,060
You can watch whenever you want

51
00:01:51,060 --> 00:01:52,500
Call me and I'll be there

52
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:54,020
I have my own security booth

53
00:01:54,103 --> 00:01:59,103
I rent a 20-square-meter apartment

54
00:01:59,103 --> 00:02:03,403
I agree, I agree.

55
00:02:03,403 --> 00:02:05,533
I totally agree.

56
00:02:05,563 --> 00:02:06,643
Oh, exactly!

57
00:02:06,643 --> 00:02:07,673
Oh!

58
00:02:07,683 --> 00:02:08,943
No—

59
00:02:08,943 --> 00:02:10,283
Be a bit sarcastic

60
00:02:10,283 --> 00:02:11,523
What are you doing?

61
00:02:11,523 --> 00:02:13,163
You still don't believe it.

62
00:02:13,163 --> 00:02:14,813
That's exactly right.

63
00:02:14,813 --> 00:02:15,373
Perfect.

64
00:02:15,373 --> 00:02:15,953
What do you want now?

65
00:02:15,953 --> 00:02:17,853
Wow, a whole twenty square metres!

66
00:02:17,853 --> 00:02:18,653
Right, right.

67
00:02:18,653 --> 00:02:19,153
Exactly.

68
00:02:19,153 --> 00:02:20,753
Twenty square metres!

69
00:02:20,753 --> 00:02:22,193
Exactly.

70
00:02:22,193 --> 00:02:24,073
Wow, so huge!

71
00:02:24,073 --> 00:02:25,693
Right—keep going.

72
00:02:25,693 --> 00:02:27,573
Just enough for me.

73
00:02:27,573 --> 00:02:29,013
Enough for both of us?

74
00:02:29,013 --> 00:02:30,723
Sure—one bedroom, one living room, one bathroom.

75
00:02:30,733 --> 00:02:33,013
I also have a soft double bed

76
00:02:33,013 --> 00:02:36,013
Yeah. Enough room for two pairs of slippers?

77
00:02:36,013 --> 00:02:36,893
Is there?

78
00:02:36,893 --> 00:02:38,053
Two pairs of slippers

79
00:02:38,053 --> 00:02:39,213
Ask it deadpan.

80
00:02:39,213 --> 00:02:39,893
There is.

81
00:02:39,893 --> 00:02:42,783
Haha

82
00:02:42,870 --> 00:02:43,710
Do you have a car?

83
00:02:43,710 --> 00:02:44,990
Yes

84
00:02:44,990 --> 00:02:47,990
I have an old-fashioned bicycle

85
00:02:47,990 --> 00:02:49,350
The kind with a crossbar

86
00:02:49,350 --> 00:02:50,190
Now I agree even more.

87
00:02:50,190 --> 00:02:52,670
I can take you to and from work.

88
00:02:52,670 --> 00:02:54,360
I love bicycles.

89
00:02:54,370 --> 00:02:55,190
Exactly.

90
00:02:55,190 --> 00:02:57,190
When I was little, my grandpa carried me

91
00:02:57,190 --> 00:02:59,710
on his bike to kindergarten.

92
00:02:59,710 --> 00:03:00,950
Ha

93
00:03:00,950 --> 00:03:03,667
Maybe you can take me back to childhood

94
00:03:05,150 --> 00:03:05,710
At her.

95
00:03:05,710 --> 00:03:07,300
You're going to insult her, right?

96
00:03:07,300 --> 00:03:08,470
Anything goes. Insult her—go.

97
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:13,130
Aren't you good at that?

98
00:03:13,130 --> 00:03:14,670
How come you've got nothing to say now?

99
00:03:14,670 --> 00:03:16,310
What's going on?

100
00:03:16,310 --> 00:03:16,937
Why?

101
00:03:16,970 --> 00:03:17,930
A loser.

102
00:03:17,930 --> 00:03:20,690
Why does "loser" sound so mild?

103
00:03:20,690 --> 00:03:21,890
Yeah, it isn't harsh enough.

104
00:03:21,890 --> 00:03:22,730
Really?

105
00:03:22,730 --> 00:03:26,340
[unclear]—you're just...

106
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:28,080
You're a fucking idiot.

107
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:31,470
You're a loser.

108
00:03:31,470 --> 00:03:33,820
"Fucking idiot" sounds mild too.

109
00:03:33,820 --> 00:03:35,760
You're a hick.

110
00:03:35,760 --> 00:03:39,872
"Hick" doesn't sound mild.

111
00:03:39,890 --> 00:03:42,237
"Hick" doesn't sound mild.

112
00:03:42,270 --> 00:03:46,350
I don't want to sit on a bicycle

113
00:03:46,350 --> 00:03:47,670
with you holding me.

114
00:03:47,670 --> 00:03:49,790
I'm worried I'll fall off.

115
00:03:49,790 --> 00:03:51,400
I don't want to squeeze in with you

116
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:53,040
in a twenty-square-metre apartment

117
00:03:53,040 --> 00:03:55,080
with room for only two pairs of slippers.

118
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:57,160
You could fit your sneakers too.

119
00:03:57,160 --> 00:03:58,620
I have a shoe rack.

120
00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:00,200
I want a yard,

121
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:01,900
where I can keep a dog and a cat,

122
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:03,070
Can you do that?

123
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:08,280
But weren't you

124
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:10,240
just talking to me so nicely?

125
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:12,590
How else

126
00:04:12,590 --> 00:04:14,130
would you have believed me?

127
00:04:14,130 --> 00:04:16,270
You're so naive.

128
00:04:16,360 --> 00:04:18,920
But you only have eight hours,

129
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:20,220
I'm trying to save you,

130
00:04:20,220 --> 00:04:22,360
You're about to be restarted.

131
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:27,060
I think...

132
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:29,597
Even if I get restarted,

133
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:31,497
I still wouldn't be with you.

134
00:04:31,534 --> 00:04:33,454
I'm doing just fine, aren't I?

135
00:04:33,454 --> 00:04:35,494
Waiter, get me a steak.

136
00:04:35,494 --> 00:04:37,424
The waiter comes over all smarmy:

137
00:04:37,434 --> 00:04:38,074
What did he say?

138
00:04:38,074 --> 00:04:40,034
Sorry, sir, this is a couples' restaurant,

139
00:04:40,034 --> 00:04:40,874
we don't sell half portions.

140
00:04:40,874 --> 00:04:45,405
Then you lose it and start swearing.

141
00:04:45,464 --> 00:04:47,214
"Bullshit! Fuck your mom!"

142
00:04:47,224 --> 00:04:50,384
What? I'm on a date, aren't I?

143
00:04:50,384 --> 00:04:51,904
Then who the fuck is that in front of me?

144
00:04:51,904 --> 00:04:54,494
The waiter says, "Sir, wake up—

145
00:04:54,494 --> 00:04:55,454
that's you."

146
00:04:55,454 --> 00:04:58,724
So you can use that mirror.

147
00:04:58,724 --> 00:04:59,754
Those mirrors can...

148
00:05:00,290 --> 00:05:02,650
These questions have never crossed my mind.

149
00:05:02,650 --> 00:05:04,040
I don't know how to respond.

150
00:05:04,050 --> 00:05:06,290
Honestly, I don't understand him at all.

151
00:05:06,290 --> 00:05:09,410
After he asked those questions,

152
00:05:09,410 --> 00:05:15,570
he felt like a stranger to me.

153
00:05:15,570 --> 00:05:18,560
Like a poor little animal, soaked by the roadside.

154
00:05:18,570 --> 00:05:21,570
Leave me there and your conscience will condemn you.

155
00:05:21,570 --> 00:05:23,560
Yeah, yeah, I think that's it.

156
00:05:23,570 --> 00:05:25,570
Maybe my perspective leans more toward...

157
00:05:25,580 --> 00:05:26,580
seeing her as a little animal.

158
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:29,580
Because we're discussing the female viewer's perspective, right?

159
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:31,637
But I think my perspective leans more toward...

160
00:05:31,637 --> 00:05:34,117
He's very innocent—not as mature as you all.

161
00:05:34,117 --> 00:05:36,117
It's different from women's and men's perspectives.

162
00:05:36,117 --> 00:05:38,507
I feel like this guy

163
00:05:38,517 --> 00:05:41,017
came into this conversation thinking,

164
00:05:41,017 --> 00:05:43,007
"This relationship feels unequal to me."

165
00:05:43,017 --> 00:05:45,817
It's not about imbalance. His love is pure.

166
00:05:45,817 --> 00:05:48,817
It is unequal. It definitely is.

167
00:05:48,817 --> 00:05:50,817
It's just that I love you, but you don't love me as much.

168
00:05:50,817 --> 00:05:52,817
You don't love me the way I love you.

169
00:05:52,817 --> 00:05:53,817
To me, that's an imbalance.

170
00:05:53,817 --> 00:05:56,204
That's his way of seeking love.

171
00:05:58,174 --> 00:05:59,324
Never validates me.

172
00:05:59,324 --> 00:06:06,374
Always acts so superior.

173
00:06:06,374 --> 00:06:06,804
Sometimes—

174
00:06:06,831 --> 00:06:11,741
Once I choose to be with you,

175
00:06:11,741 --> 00:06:14,911
I feel a sense of responsibility.

176
00:06:14,911 --> 00:06:17,111
No matter what happens,

177
00:06:17,111 --> 00:06:19,931
unless I turn out to be a scumbag

178
00:06:19,931 --> 00:06:22,791
and run off with somebody else.

179
00:06:22,791 --> 00:06:26,431
I'm not really that rich.

180
00:06:26,431 --> 00:06:29,973
What I can do for you right now

181
00:06:30,251 --> 00:06:31,211
is honestly

182
00:06:31,211 --> 00:06:33,768
the most

183
00:06:33,781 --> 00:06:34,871
I can give.

184
00:06:34,871 --> 00:06:37,501
I've never asked you for anything.

185
00:06:37,501 --> 00:06:39,561
I've never once said,

186
00:06:39,561 --> 00:06:42,041
"You're my girlfriend.
You should give me gifts."

187
00:06:42,041 --> 00:06:44,501
We just started dating.
